 \section{EM, Gravity, Diagnostics, Relativity, and Inertia Research Tracks}
+\subsection{Maxwell-inspired target-blind mechanical closure falsifier}
+\label{sec:rt_maxwell_blind_mechanical_falsifier}
+
+\paragraph{Status and scope.}
+\textbf{[ORTHODOX HISTORICAL INPUT / RESEARCH-TRACK SST TEST].}
+In \emph{On Physical Lines of Force}, Maxwell decomposes an axisymmetric state
+of stress into hydrostatic pressure plus an axial pressure/tension, proposes a
+molecular-vortex illustration for the resulting pressure anisotropy, derives the
+similarity scale $\Delta p\propto\rho v^2$, later introduces the ``reduced
+momentum'' of a mechanical system as the quantity whose time derivative gives
+the force associated with changing motion, and treats changing electric
+displacement as a current-like contribution \cite{Maxwell1861PhysicalLines}.
+None of Maxwell's literal cell or idle-wheel microphysics is adopted here.
+
+The purpose of this section is to turn those structural ideas into negative
+SST tests with no target-dependent coefficient fitting.
+
+\subsubsection{Gate M1: coarse-grained kinetic swirl stress}
+
+\textbf{[ORTHODOX COARSE-GRAINING / DEFINITION].}
+For a preregistered linear coarse-graining operator at scale $\ell$, define
+\begin{align}
+    R_{ij}^{(\ell)}
+    :=
+    \rhoF\left(
+    \overline{u_i u_j}^{\,(\ell)}
+    -
+    \bar u_i^{\,(\ell)}\bar u_j^{\,(\ell)}
+    \right).
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_Rij}
+\end{align}
+This is the resolved kinetic/momentum-flux covariance familiar from
+coarse-grained fluid mechanics \cite{Reynolds1895}.  It is not a replacement for
+the primitive inviscid Cauchy stress $-p\delta_{ij}$.
+
+On the support where
+$\|\bar{\boldsymbol\omega}\|>\omega_{\rm floor}$, define
+\begin{align}
+    \mathbf n_\omega
+    &=
+    \frac{\bar{\boldsymbol\omega}}
+    {\|\bar{\boldsymbol\omega}\|},
+    \\
+    p_\parallel
+    &=n_iR_{ij}^{(\ell)}n_j,
+    \\
+    p_\perp
+    &=\frac{\operatorname{tr}R^{(\ell)}-p_\parallel}{2},
+    \\
+    \Delta p_\omega
+    &=p_\perp-p_\parallel.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_pressure_split}
+\end{align}
+The best axisymmetric projection about the declared vorticity director is
+\begin{align}
+    R_{ij}^{\rm ax}
+    =
+    p_\perp\delta_{ij}
+    +
+    (p_\parallel-p_\perp)n_i n_j.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_Rax}
+\end{align}
+Define the local normalized tensor residual
+\begin{align}
+    \epsilon_\sigma
+    :=
+    \frac{\|R^{(\ell)}-R^{\rm ax}\|_F}
+    {\max(\|R^{(\ell)}\|_F,R_{\rm floor})},
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_eps_sigma}
+\end{align}
+and, with $\mathbf e_{\min}$ the normalized eigenvector of the smallest
+eigenvalue of $R^{(\ell)}$,
+\begin{align}
+    a_\omega
+    :=
+    |\mathbf n_\omega\cdot\mathbf e_{\min}|.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_alignment}
+\end{align}
+
+\textbf{[PREREGISTERED FALSIFIER].}
+Using the top $80\%$ of the nonzero coarse-vorticity support after the declared
+boundary trim, the campaign requires
+\begin{align}
+    \operatorname{median}(\epsilon_\sigma)&\le0.20,
+    &
+    \operatorname{median}(a_\omega)&\ge0.90,
+    &
+    \Pr(\Delta p_\omega>0)&\ge0.80.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_local_gates}
+\end{align}
+Failure of any one of these conditions rejects the single-axis Maxwell-like
+coarse-stress closure for that declared filter family.
+
+\subsubsection{Gate M2: blind similarity exponents}
+
+For each geometrically similar case, preregister before computation the density
+$\rhoF$, a velocity scale $v_{\rm ref}$, and a common geometry scale $L$.  The
+analysis fits
+\begin{align}
+    \ln\Delta p_\omega
+    =
+    b_0
+    +b_\rho\ln\rhoF
+    +b_v\ln v_{\rm ref}
+    +b_L\ln L
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_log_scaling}
+\end{align}
+without constraining the coefficients.  The frozen gates are
+\begin{align}
+    0.85&\le b_\rho\le1.15,
+    &
+    1.80&\le b_v\le2.20,
+    &
+    -0.25&\le b_L\le0.25,
+    &
+    R^2&\ge0.98.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_scaling_thresholds}
+\end{align}
+A density sweep may be performed as an off-canon similarity test of the
+resolved equations; it is not a proposal to vary the canonical physical value
+of $\rhoF$.
+
+The dimensionless reported coefficient is
+\begin{align}
+    C_{\rm blind}
+    :=
+    \frac{\operatorname{median}(\Delta p_\omega)}
+    {\rhoF v_{\rm ref}^2}.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_C}
+\end{align}
+\textbf{[BLINDNESS GUARD].}
+No numerical target for $C_{\rm blind}$ participates in M1 or M2.  After the
+blind report is frozen, Maxwell's special uniform circular-vortex value
+$C=1/4$ may be opened as a historical comparison, while the ordinary
+Euler/Bernoulli scale $C=1/2$ may be opened as a second comparison.  Neither is
+a pass/fail target for an arbitrary SST finite-core profile
+\cite{Maxwell1861PhysicalLines,Saffman1992}.
+
+\subsubsection{Gate M3: handedness and angular-momentum null}
+
+Maxwell explicitly noted that the force scale in his similarity argument could
+be independent of vortex diameter while the angular momentum need not be.
+For preregistered opposite-handed realizations with identical geometry and
+$|v_{\rm ref}|$, define
+\begin{align}
+    \epsilon_L
+    &:={
+    \|\mathbf L_+ + \mathbf L_-\|
+    \over
+    \max(\|\mathbf L_+\|+\|\mathbf L_-\|,L_{\rm floor})},
+    \\
+    \epsilon_{\Delta p}
+    &:={
+    |\Delta p_{\omega,+}-\Delta p_{\omega,-}|
+    \over
+    \max(|\Delta p_{\omega,+}|,|\Delta p_{\omega,-}|,p_{\rm floor})}.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_handedness_nulls}
+\end{align}
+The blind gates are
+\begin{align}
+    \epsilon_L\le0.05,
+    \qquad
+    \epsilon_{\Delta p}\le0.05.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_handedness_thresholds}
+\end{align}
+Thus angular momentum is required to reverse while the quadratic stress channel
+remains even under swirl reversal.  A claimed isotropic ensemble must in
+addition demonstrate cancellation of its net bulk angular momentum rather than
+assuming it.
+
+\subsubsection{Gate M4: reduced momentum as an independently reconstructed channel}
+
+\textbf{[BRIDGE / THEOREM TARGET].}
+Maxwell's reduced-momentum construction motivates, but does not prove, an SST
+factorization.  The test requires three quantities computed by independent
+solver routes:
+\begin{enumerate}
+    \item $\mathbf u$: material/coherent velocity;
+    \item $\mathbf p_{\rm red}$: reduced dynamical momentum obtained from a
+    declared action derivative, generalized impulse, or equivalent independent
+    dynamical response;
+    \item $\mathbf A$: independently evolved transverse/effective potential.
+\end{enumerate}
+It is invalid to construct $\mathbf p_{\rm red}$ from $m_e\mathbf u$ or to
+construct $\mathbf A$ from $(m_e/e)\mathbf u$ and then claim this gate as an
+independent test.
+
+On a deterministic preregistered $60/40$ train/validation split, fit scalar
+through-origin maps
+\begin{align}
+    \mathbf p_{\rm red}
+    &=\beta_u\mathbf u+\mathbf r_u,
+    \\
+    \mathbf A
+    &=\beta_p\mathbf p_{\rm red}+\mathbf r_p,
+    \\
+    \mathbf A
+    &=\beta_A\mathbf u+\mathbf r_A.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_reduced_fits}
+\end{align}
+Each relation must satisfy on held-out data
+\begin{align}
+    \operatorname{NRMSE}_{\rm val}&\le0.05,
+    &
+    \operatorname{median}|\cos\theta|&\ge0.995,
+    &
+    \operatorname{CV}(\beta\mid\text{group})&\le0.05,
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_reduced_thresholds}
+\end{align}
+and the independently fitted coefficients must satisfy
+\begin{align}
+    { |\beta_A-\beta_p\beta_u| \over |\beta_A| }
+    \le0.05.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_factorization_gate}
+\end{align}
+The numerical electron target remains sealed during fitting.  Only after the
+blind files are frozen is the committed comparison
+\begin{align}
+    \beta_A
+    \stackrel{?}{=}
+    \frac{m_e}{e}
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_unblind_A_target}
+\end{align}
+opened, with a preregistered relative tolerance of $5\%$.  This is a test of the
+existing SI normalization bridge, not a derivation of charge or electron mass.
+
+\subsubsection{Gate M5: optional structural displacement-current closure}
+
+\textbf{[SPECULATIVE / OPTIONAL FALSIFIER].}
+A structural displacement field is admissible only if it is defined independently
+of the Ampere residual being fitted.  Let
+\begin{align}
+    \mathbf Y
+    :=
+    \nabla\times\mathbf H
+    -
+    \mathbf J_{\rm transport}.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_ampere_residual}
+\end{align}
+The target-blind fit is
+\begin{align}
+    \mathbf Y
+    =
+    \lambda_D\,\partial_t\mathbf D_{\rm struct}
+    +
+    \mathbf r_D.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_storage_fit}
+\end{align}
+The coefficient $\lambda_D$ is fitted on alternating training times and is not
+predicted in advance.  Held-out data require
+\begin{align}
+    \operatorname{NRMSE}_{\rm val}&\le0.20,
+    &
+    R^2_{\rm val}&\ge0.90,
+    &
+    1-\frac{\operatorname{RMS}(\mathbf r_D)}
+    {\operatorname{RMS}(\mathbf Y)}&\ge0.80.
+    \label{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_storage_thresholds}
+\end{align}
+Failure rejects the declared storage variable; it does not justify adding a new
+source term by hand.
+
+\subsubsection{Blind protocol and verdict}
+
+\textbf{[RESEARCH / PREREGISTRATION].}
+The executable protocol freezes before the production run:
+\begin{enumerate}
+    \item filter fraction and boundary trim;
+    \item active-vorticity support rule;
+    \item $v_{\rm ref}$ and geometry-scale definitions;
+    \item train/validation split seed;
+    \item all numerical gates in
+    Eqs.~\eqref{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_local_gates},
+    \eqref{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_scaling_thresholds},
+    \eqref{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_handedness_thresholds},
+    \eqref{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_reduced_thresholds}, and
+    \eqref{eq:rt_maxwell_blind_factorization_gate};
+    \item SHA-256 commitments to the hidden comparison targets.
+\end{enumerate}
+
+The decision language is:
+\begin{center}
+\begin{tabular}{ll}
+\hline
+\textbf{FAIL} & any mandatory preregistered gate fails;\\
+\textbf{INCONCLUSIVE} & required independent data or scan rank is missing;\\
+\textbf{PASS} & every mandatory blind gate passes.\\
+\hline
+\end{tabular}
+\end{center}
+A PASS supports only this closure class.  It does not establish SST, does not
+validate Maxwell's molecular cells, and does not collapse the material Euler
+sector into the independent photon/link sector.
+
 
